+A push from the primary checkout ends with a read of `.git/index.lock`: a
+zero-byte lock born in the pre-push hook's last steps outlived one push and
+blocked two peers' commits before its own seat saw it (2026-09-25); a lock that
+outlives the push with no holder is the pusher's to report at once.
+
 The advisory commit queue, `git:index/head` active claim, and shared-log
 entry are the coordination surfaces; the lock file is never one of them.
 
